 "outro": "Next: the Resonance Loom. The ship has stopped rehearsing.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [6, 29],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "SIGNAL HOUSE",
   "text": "Calder, there's no roof left: the ship tore it open to sing at the sky. Something sits at the far end, and it's why the gate is sealed."
  },
  {
   "id": "nave",
   "at": [20, 29],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Two galleries, north and south, with singers on both. The pillars stop a round. Don't cross this floor in a straight line."
  },
  {
   "id": "shell",
   "at": [44, 29],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "Shells on legs. A round does almost nothing to the front of one. It opens its shell to hit you: that is when to shoot, or to circle it, or to throw a bell-breaker over it."
  },
  {
   "id": "mother",
   "at": [58, 29],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "She is weeping, and where it lands it burns and slows you: walk out of it. Something is swelling on her skirt. Kill her and the gate will open."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [30, 10],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "One rib of this wall is thin. A held breath, behind it."
  },
  {
   "id": "gate",
   "at": [79, 29],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "SIGNAL HOUSE",
   "text": "The gate is open. Past it the ship goes on singing, but it's quieter."
  }
